                    '**Note on MikroTik and compatibility:** In modern versions of MikroTik RouterOS (v7+), `/31` is natively supported. However, on legacy versions (v6 and older) or when adjacency fails, configuring `/31` directly breaks connectivity. Many operators incorrectly resort to configuring a `/24` or `/30` mask. The professional solution is to configure the local address as `/32` and define the `network` parameter with the exact IP of the remote peer, establishing the point-to-point adjacency without wasting IP address space.'
